  "question": {
    "text": "The solubility of barium iodate in an aqueous solution prepared by mixing 200 mL of 0.010 M barium nitrate with 100 mL of 0.10 M sodium iodate is $\\boldsymbol{X} \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{~mol} \\mathrm{dm}^{-3}$. The value of $\\boldsymbol{X}$ is $\\qquad$ .\nUse: Solubility product constant $\\left(K_{\\mathrm{sp}}\\right)$ of barium iodate $=1.58 \\times 10^{-9}$"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "3.95",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"assets\\st0000_bc0540c0d598.png\"><br>$\\left[\\mathrm{NaIO}_3\\right]=\\frac{6}{300}=2 \\times 10^{-2} \\mathrm{M}$<br>$\\begin{aligned} \\mathrm{Ba}\\left(\\mathrm{IO}_3\\right)_2(\\mathrm{~s}) \\rightleftharpoons \\mathrm{Ba}^{2+}+ & 2 \\mathrm{IO}_3^{-} \\\\ \\mathrm{s} \\qquad & \\left(2 \\times 10^{-2}+2 \\mathrm{~s}\\right)\\end{aligned}$<br>$\\begin{aligned} & \\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{sp}}=\\left[\\mathrm{Ba}^{+2}\\right]\\left[\\mathrm{IO}_3^{-}\\right]^2 \\\\ & 1.58 \\times 10^{-9}=\\left[\\mathrm{Ba}^{+2}\\right] \\times\\left(2 \\times 10^{-2}\\right)^2 \\\\ & {\\left[\\mathrm{Ba}^{+2}\\right]=\\mathrm{s}=3.95 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{M}} \\\\ & \\mathrm{X}=3.95\\end{aligned}$"
  }
